A||||14||Spektrum-87GT||rarely asked question about engine swaps||||1||
Z||000000||Spektrum-87GT||09-26-2001||07:54 PM||||ok, i know a LOT of questions have been asked in the past about engine swaps... but i've got a little off the wall one... of the 3.4, 3800 series II(and supercharged), sbc, and lt1 engine swaps... which is the most reliable? This has to be my daily driver... looking to spend ~4000, have a 5 speed getrag, looking for ~250hp. Thinking a s/c 3800 is going to be my best bet but not sure if i'll be able to do it for under 4k, anyone else have any suggestions?||||reg||1
Z||000001||jelly2m8||09-26-2001||08:22 PM||||actually all those engines are extremely reliable. The SBC's and 2nd gen 3800's for sure. the 3.4L is basically a 60* V6, so we know that is pretty reliable. I havent owned a LT1, but that again is basically a SBC.<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GTZ34||09-26-2001||10:04 PM||||enh-enh I'm sorry that question has been asked before.  I'd tell you go search but will save you the trouble.  Each owner that has the repsective swap in their car claims that their swap is the most reliable.  Yes, believe it or not its true.  In my opinion, it comes down to the skill level of the person(s) doing the swap and quality level of the hardware.||||reg||1
Z||000003||foxgapfiero||09-26-2001||10:05 PM||||I just put a 3.4 in over Labor Day weekend as a daily driver. I love it. The car seems much more agile and resposive. I'm running 19# injectors and Joe Wynmans prom. 18mpg around town.<P>------------------<BR>Mark Hoagland<BR>86GT 3.4<BR>88GT T-Top<BR>85GT caddy v-8 next swap<BR>84SE trailer next project||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowCG||09-27-2001||11:45 PM||||The most reliable will be the one with the least amount of torque to tear up your small diameter clutch,engine mounts,cradle.<BR>The only engine that'll make around 250hp is the 3.4 tdc;those were the numbers I was searching for with the same reasons.||||reg||1
Z||000005||GTMike||09-28-2001||03:37 AM||||why did you need a new prom for the 3.4.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula88||09-28-2001||09:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lowCG:<BR><B>The only engine that'll make around 250hp is the 3.4 tdc;those were the numbers I was searching for with the same reasons.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Um, 3800SC is 240HP stock, does that count? How about a TPI SBC?  That should be able to get about 250HP pretty easy.   <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Alex4mula||09-28-2001||11:28 AM||||I heard that Wynmans PROM is used in 3.4s for the 19# injectors and some other tweaking.||||reg||1
Z||000008||DKOV||09-28-2001||01:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B> Um, 3800SC is 240HP stock, does that count?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Now THAT'S funny!  a 3800 SUPERCHARGED is STOCK  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Take away that supercharger and THEN you get stock.  And what's that?  Around 160HP?<P>Supercharge a 3.4 (apples to apples right?) and what do you get?  325HP?  350HP?<P>I'm was pulling +250HP out of my 3.4 TDC with only minor mods like better air, better exhaust and better plugs.  With mods, like the ported/polished intake, custom exhaust, etc.  I'm cracking 300.<P>The best news is, it IS reliable!  This car is a track killer as well as a daily.<P>To this day, eveyone still asks me why I didn't go with a V8 if I wanted all that HP.  Honestly, I don't know except that I LOVE this car with this motor.<P>It's the very best thing I ever did for my Fiero...  Well, one of them anyway  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>DKOV -<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||87GTZ34||09-28-2001||02:27 PM||||DKOV,  actually your mistaken.  Pontiac ships a 3800 super charged engine 'stock' from the factory.  No add ons once you've purchased the car.  It sounds like what you meant was normally aspirated.||||reg||1
Z||000010||BV MotorSports||09-28-2001||10:52 PM||||Just a few notes on the LT1.<BR>93-94 use a non-vented opti-spark (distributor) these will die w/o warning.<BR>95-up are vented and MUCH cheaper to buy. Like 260 vrs 400+! you can swap the non vented to vented but it requires a few items that GM sells as a kit.<BR>96 and up are OBDII. You can use a 94-95 ECM and remove all the added OBDII stuff w/o triggering the SES light.<BR>Snaderson Headers makes a set of nice "D" port headers for the LT1 that can be used for the Fiero swap.<BR>93 use a speed density F/I. Does not respond to mods as well as later model LT1's.<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 89mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>87 Conquest TSi 406 SBC V8!<BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
Z||000011||BV MotorSports||09-28-2001||10:56 PM||||Oh BTW Spektrum...come out to Langley Speedway THIS Sat. night @ 7pm and watch me and my Fiero GT compete in the Night of Champions race! Tonight there was a NSX and he was whooping booty! I told my wife that when I end up running that car tomorrow to take a pic just off the line....thats probably the only time I will be in front of him!<BR>Come on out!<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 89mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>87 Conquest TSi 406 SBC V8!<BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||14
Z||000012||DKOV||09-28-2001||11:19 PM||||87GTX34...<P>Yeah, that was my joking point  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Comparing a stock 3.4 to a stock 3.8.  Yes, the factory sends it "from the factory" with a SC, but they don't ALL come with them... the SC is a "hop-up" (and a mighty GOOD one too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) while the 3.4 didn't.<P>Just like the 3.1 engines... "stock" and "with Turbo".  But with the 3.1, adding the Turbo only made 205HP.  Again, the 3.4 motor was stronger "stock".<P>I can't help it... If I COULD get a SC or a Turbo on my 3.4 I definitely would!  Only, I have TWO issues...  Reliability and WHERE AM I GONNA PUT ONE?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Gotta love the 3.4!<P>DKOV -||||reg||1
